To make Bootstrap tables sortable alphanumerically without using jQuery or other plugins, you can use the HTML5 Drag and Drop API. Here’s a step-by-step guide:

1. **HTML Structure**: Ensure your table has a structure that supports sorting. Each header cell (`<th>`) should have a unique identifier or class to handle the sorting logic.

2. **CSS Styling**: Add some basic CSS to style the table and the headers. For example, you can add a class to the headers to indicate they are sortable.

3. **JavaScript Logic**: Use the HTML5 Drag and Drop API to handle the sorting. Here’s a basic example:

```html
<table class="table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th draggable="true" id="header1">Name</th>
      <th draggable="true" id="header2">Age</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>John</td>
      <td>25</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Jane</td>
      <td>30</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<script>
  const headers = document.querySelectorAll('th[draggable="true"]');
  const rows = document.querySelectorAll('tbody tr');

  headers.forEach(header => {
    header.addEventListener('dragstart', (e) => {
      e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', e.target.id);
    });
  });

  rows.forEach(row => {
    row.addEventListener('dragover', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
    });

    row.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const headerId = e.dataTransfer.getData('text/plain');
      const header = document.getElementById(headerId);
      const column = header.nextElementSibling;

      // Sort the rows based on the column
      const sortedRows = Array.from(rows).sort((a, b) => {
        const aValue = a.querySelector(column).textContent;
        const bValue = b.querySelector(column).textContent;
        return aValue.localeCompare(bValue);
      });

      sortedRows.forEach(row => row.parentNode.appendChild(row));
    });
  });
</script>
```

This code sets up a basic sortable table where you can drag and drop rows to sort them alphanumerically based on the clicked header.

