The `draggable` attribute in the table headers is used to enable the HTML5 Drag and Drop API. When set to `true`, it allows the user to drag the header, which triggers the `dragstart` event. This event is used to store the ID of the header being dragged, which is then used to determine the column to sort by.

How does the `dragstart` event work in this context?

The `dragstart` event is triggered when the user starts dragging an element. In this context, it is used to store the ID of the header being dragged. This is done using `e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', e.target.id)`. When the user drops the header on a row, the `drop` event is triggered, and the stored ID is retrieved using `e.dataTransfer.getData('text/plain')`. This ID is then used to identify the column to sort by.

